# Ellipse Engine — two perpendicular ellipses from one motor
# Adapted from the supplied Quickstroke finite-program guard pattern.
# Copyright (c) 2026 Christian Ströbele (CrispStrobe).
# SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
# Reset/reload the saved model before starting. Connect its motor to hub A.
# The motor travels with the upper carriage; the lower carriage is passive.
# One uninterrupted three-turn move traces both ellipses three times.
# Reversing retraces the same paths, then returns to the saved encoder datum.
# All speeds are degrees per second. No ellipse coordinates drive the physics.
# This is a Robot Lab simulation program, not downloadable hub firmware.
DEVICE SPIKE

WHEN flag clicked:
  lab start
  lab stop motor A hold
  wait 0.5 seconds
  IF (abs of (0 - (lab motor A angle))) > 2 THEN:
    lab stop motor A hold
    stop all
  lab run motor A for (1080 - (lab motor A angle)) degrees at 30 degrees per second
  lab stop motor A hold
  IF (abs of (1080 - (lab motor A angle))) > 2 THEN:
    lab stop motor A hold
    stop all
  wait 1.5 seconds
  IF (abs of (1080 - (lab motor A angle))) > 2 THEN:
    lab stop motor A hold
    stop all
  lab run motor A for (0 - (lab motor A angle)) degrees at 30 degrees per second
  lab stop motor A hold
  IF (abs of (0 - (lab motor A angle))) > 2 THEN:
    lab stop motor A hold
    stop all
  wait 1.5 seconds
  IF (abs of (0 - (lab motor A angle))) > 2 THEN:
    lab stop motor A hold
    stop all
  lab stop motor A hold
